+## Diagnosing configuration
+
+Run `python -m payhook doctor` to print every setting with its effective value and where it came from (`env`, `.env` or `default`), plus the `.env` path it looked at. Secret values (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are never printed; only whether they are set and their length is shown. The output is safe to paste into a support ticket.
+
+`python -m payhook check` prints only the names of missing required settings.
 
